you  the SE 2d grid shell is an open-air  pavilion that was built as an extension  of the a CTD library so it's an open-air  structure that doubles as as work space  for the library but it also serves a  second purpose of posting a CTD events  get-togethers and dinners so the project  actually started as a student workshop  the students worked in teams for two  weeks came up with some design proposals  and it was society that one team's idea  of doing a grid shelf was innovative and  interesting and so after that we worked  for about nine months on the design of  this place there were indeed some  significant challenges along the way one  of them which was making sure that  everything fits at the end we had  basically just only one construction  drawing which was sort of a numeric map  that indicated where each piece goes the  contractors simply followed that map and  pieced the whole ritual together like a  puzzle  I think personally that one of the  interesting things about the grid shell  is that it's entirely made in Singapore  it was a pretty major production process  that involved over a hundred people in  various roles we tried to wrap that  whole geometrical solution to the  software but others can use it really  resulted a new way of building  structures these projects always  teamwork and you can't do it alone  we had very nice relationship with our  engineers our client plus fabricators  builders I think the president Design  Award is a wonderful annual celebration  of design in Singapore it points out  things that are already well-known and  highly celebrated and other times it  puts the spotlight on projects that  people don't know very much about but by  giving an award to such project and  draws a lot more people to pay attention  to them I think it's also important for  designers to pick what they individually  are really good at and really push  themselves in becoming even better at  that this is the SE TD great shelf  design of the air  you

